WEBVTT

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:42.390
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:49.570
I'm watching an endless dream

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:56.030
Aren't you watching too?

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:03.370
It's always close by no matter how far away it seems

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.210
Can't you see it too?

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:15.680
The things you can't normally say

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.390
The things you try to express

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.890
The things you're willing to fight for

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:26.600
Standing on your own two feet

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:33.280
The night sky illuminates them all

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:40.410
The first flash of lightning

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:46.750
This is our battle to fight

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:54.090
It's why I'm going to live in this town

00:01:54.380 --> 00:02:02.600
This dream will absolutely come true

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:14.320
You're here early, Inspector Ando.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.650
Bear in mind, HQ has overridden your prohibition

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.780
of Salty Dog from the control room.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.330
I'm aware.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.290
I've been informed that Mutou Hana's precognitive abilities have been lost.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:35.170
That makes the Independent Attack Force your plan requires

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.670
effectively useless per your own mistake.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.140
I'll be blunt.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.390
We're extremely skeptical of the Midsummer's Knights'

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.980
practical utilities.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.150
That's rather harsh.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.980
There are also rumors that

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:59.820
the Intercept Faction has an even more foolish operation in preparation.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.700
Then I'll be blunt, as well.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:06.620
There are some rather nasty rumors that you've been sent

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.670
to the Tanegashima base to capture Mutou Hana.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.540
Well, even if those ugly accusations were true...

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:19.720
She unfortunately isn't here.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:46.700
How are you finding the <i>Tenkaido</i>? To your liking?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:49.250
Everyone's so nice.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.000
How are the people in Tanegashima?

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.870
They're all good people.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:55.590
Is she really that naïve?

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.210
Is there a boy you like?

00:03:58.500 --> 00:03:59.710
The captain!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.380
Manatsu Daichi, eh?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:06.800
Hey, do you know the boy who pilots the Nebula Engine?

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:07.470
Teppei?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:08.390
Yeah!

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.810
Arashi Teppei.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.430
He's pretty cute, isn't he?

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.900
Does he have a girlfriend?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.150
I don't think he does.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.810
I see!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.990
What do we do?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.360
We have to go for it!

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.610
Should we?

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.070
When will he be here next?

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.740
I wonder how the others are doing...

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.540
Ta-da!

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.840
Snack time!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:42.090
Nice!

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.300
I'm so glad everyone's feeling better.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.510
Yeah!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.690
Spitz to Doghouse.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.030
Mutou Hana is not currently at the Tanegashima base.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:09.330
Mutou Hana, pilot of the Flare Engine who defeated the Kill-T-Gang Type-5,

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.120
is evidently aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:12.870
Over.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.420
Our agent aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i> has sent us nothing to indicate that.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.590
We've been had.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:26.180
Nishikubo arranged all of this to hide Mutou Hana.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:32.270
Those Midsummer's Knights are quite irritating.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.560
They've proven themselves adept at stalling for time, though.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.610
Cerberus, Sarama, and Garmr have all assembled.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.400
We don't need the Knights anymore.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.570
The
Midsummer's
Knights

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.040
Are you lonely without Hana?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.630
Well, there's nothing I can do about it. That's the plan.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.930
I was talking to Pitz, you know.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:15.520
There's someone who's even sadder without Hana than you are.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.440
Okay, I'll break out my healing spell for you again.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:25.360
You mean...

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.950
Belly Button Forte!

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.330
Does that work on Pitz?

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.370
I'm pretending to cast it on Pitz,

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:39.420
but I'm really using it on Daichi.

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.710
R-Really?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.130
Belly Button Forte!

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:46.550
Who are you doing that one for?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:49.970
It feels like I'm the only one not showing any skin today,

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:55.390
and my position as heroine is in danger... I think.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:04.940
Oh, sir.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.710
Then, goodbye.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.000
I'll be free tonight.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:29.800
Yes, sir.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:42.350
The light shines through the feather in my grasp

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:48.150
As if it was merrily dancing

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:53.820
I'd like our paths to cross

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:57.660
As we head towards warmth and kindness

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:05.630
Let's begin our journey

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.890
We've received reports of large numbers of people

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:18.970
simultaneously falling into comas in the Tokyo ES area.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.730
It's likely they're gathering Orgone energy again.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:33.450
Hey, Teppei, that pendant on your chest...

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.490
This?

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.330
The Blue Star.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.870
You two take turns wearing it, right?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.870
It's a game we've played since we were kids.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:49.590
Whichever one of us is able to surprise the other gets to wear it.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:51.460
I'm retaking it!

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.300
I like the way you never give up.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.470
You boys are so in love.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:02.890
Who's that?

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.020
She's with Salty Dog.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.520
An inspector?

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.490
You really are only children.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.740
If you seriously expect an Independent Attack Force

00:09:18.740 --> 00:09:20.910
comprised of entirely of children to accomplish anything,

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.660
I must question your sanity.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:28.670
Thank you, Lady Seiren.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.300
I have two capsules this time.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.420
Then one person will be staying here.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:35.840
Where are the others?

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:38.140
They're leaving it to us.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.930
We have serious teamwork issues.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:42.520
Teamwork?

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:46.560
You've been spending far too much time around the Earthlings.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.860
Lady Seiren...

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:56.860
Are you still concerned about the Earthlings?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:01.240
They aren't like us. Their lives are finite.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.250
When a finite life form gains sentience,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:10.330
a destructive desire manifests deep within its heart.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:15.880
In the end, their race's only purpose is to be consumed by us.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:21.890
You forget that our lives were once finite, as well.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.810
We've got two Orgone Capsules.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.350
Can you say "ladies first"?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.150
I don't care.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.400
What about the other one?

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.270
Let's use this to decide.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:34.980
Tails.

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:35.900
Heads.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:39.950
Heads, it is.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.240
Sorry.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.660
You weren't cheating, were you?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.790
I wouldn't do that to a comrade.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:50.750
After all, teamwork is important.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:00.050
AEOs confirmed!

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.810
The Type-2! And one we've never seen, Type-6!

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:08.270
Manifestation point is within
Defensive Zone 1, Omega sector!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.850
Activate Earth Engine and Nebula Engine
launch sequences immediately.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:12.940
Roger!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.770
Earth Engine and Nebula Engine energy levels nominal!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.740
Flare Engine's status?

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:10.780
Damaged in the last battle, and still undergoing repairs.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:12.950
You're wasting your time.

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.160
I've ordered Cerberus to launch.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.710
When?

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:20.540
Cerberus?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.800
Impactor signals in Omega sector!

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.630
They'll make contact with the Kill-T-Gangs in 80 seconds!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.510
The latest unmanned Impactors,

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:35.810
developed by the Ark Faction to support the Kivotos Plan.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.810
They've already been cleared for deployment?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:43.690
Manned Impactors are relics of the past, Science Chief.

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.860
And summer is about to end.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:50.660
Yes, the season of the Midsummer's Knights.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.580
So this is the real me?

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:58.960
Yes, I can feel the power pulsing through me!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:01.750
What's that?

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.220
Hm? They aren't the same ones as usual.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:11.680
Not that it matters, of course!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.020
These guys...

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.110
They're fast.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:29.280
Cerberus consists of three units surrounded by superconductive magnetic fields

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.030
that cause them to move chaotically.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:35.490
Magnetic levitational maneuverable Impactors.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:39.200
These unmanned weapons are far more mobile

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:41.920
and more powerful than manned Impactors.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:44.170
Cerberus, lost!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:44.920
What?

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:46.710
Was it destroyed?

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:47.380
I don't know.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.720
The signal just stopped.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.300
Video incoming.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.340
What?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:55.390
What's going on?

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.280
They've taken control of them...

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.360
Impossible.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.950
Eyecatch

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:22.290
Didn't anyone ever tell you that machines are easy to fool?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.250
Video's back online.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:29.630
Switch low-orbit Impactors to emergency mode!

00:16:29.630 --> 00:16:30.340
Wait.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:34.090
Earth and Nebula are en route to intercept.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:36.850
60 seconds until contact with the Kill-T-Gangs!

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.810
Huh? Aren't there more than usual?

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:48.650
Be careful.

00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:51.780
The enemy's taken over the new Impactors.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.360
Really?

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:55.070
Captain, they're coming!

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.580
Off you go.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.340
Captain!

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:24.600
If the enemy's controlling Cerberus too, we can't win...

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:27.350
Never thought your own dog might bite you, huh?

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.540
They're fast!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.920
Earth Engine and Nebula Engine are being pushed back.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.300
They're falling back to Defensive Zone 2.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.050
This is bad.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:58.760
It'll be okay.

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:04.140
Teppei and the captain won't lose to them.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:05.850
They won't!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:10.560
Malkin, Zimbardo, and the new Impactors, too?

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:11.860
This isn't good.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.570
You're sounding pretty wimpy, Teppei.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.990
These guys won't beat us.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:19.410
Right?

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:24.200
I like the way you never give up.

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:32.960
Teppei! Daichi!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.350
Okay!

00:18:43.350 --> 00:18:46.270
It's crazy, but they're working well together.

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:49.060
You boys are so in love...

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.230
There!

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:53.980
I've retaken Cerberus!

00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:55.280
What?

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.820
Hey, Malkin...

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:05.040
You're playing around too much!

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.290
You don't need to tell me.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:08.500
I know!

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:14.590
Lady Seiren gave me this precious energy.

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.760
I can't waste it!

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.470
I never get any better at this.

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:38.070
We're being pushed back!

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.070
What is this?

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:45.410
A back door from when the Kill-T-Gang hacked Cerberus?

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:48.620
If I can follow it...

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:52.830
If you don't order them to use the low-orbit Impactors now, it'll be too late!

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:55.040
Just believe in us!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.510
I'll hit them with my special attack spell.

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:02.090
Die, Earth Impactors!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:07.430
Captain, I'm borrowing the Earth Engine's systems.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.930
Wh-What?

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.230
Take this...

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.150
What?

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:20.610
What's going on?

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:28.700
Captain!

00:20:29.120 --> 00:20:31.000
The enemy has stopped moving!

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.160
Teppei!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:33.920
We'll destroy their Ego Blocks!

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.080
Roger!

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.360
It didn't work?

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.820
An Ego Block can only be destroyed if its owner wills it.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:07.570
At least, for now.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:14.040
Mutou Hana, I want to ask you something.

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:19.130
How can you have so much faith in them?

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:25.380
Because we're a team.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:35.270
Even if it was only for a moment,

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.810
they were able to interfere with the Kill-T-Gang's controls.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.730
It was that magical girl.

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.650
All of our attacks have been stopped.

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:48.620
Lady Seiren,

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.490
the next time we activate the Kill-T-Gangs,

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:54.960
perhaps we should all attack at once.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:01.920
Yeah! We did it!

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:05.630
Good work, you guys.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:08.930
It looked like they shut down for a moment.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:11.220
How did you do that?

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.890
I did it.

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:15.180
Am I a good girl? Am I?

00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:18.100
Inspector...

00:22:19.560 --> 00:22:21.230
I'll just say one thing.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:26.700
We won't abandon the people who live on this world,

00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:30.120
as long as we have this team.

00:22:39.290 --> 00:22:41.540
The Midsummer's Knights, huh?

00:24:13.390 --> 00:24:18.060
Teppei, Hana, and I return to Tanegashima from the <i>Tenkaido</i>

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:21.140
in the <i>Flügel</i>, an atmospheric re-entry capsule.

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:24.770
But a plot by the Ark Faction, which wants Hana,

00:24:24.770 --> 00:24:27.150
causes us to crash land in Australia.

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:30.940
And then, we're attacked by Salty Dog's weapons.

00:24:30.940 --> 00:24:33.740
Next time, on episode 18 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:35.490
Onslaught Through the Wilderness.

00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:35.490
Onslaught Through the Wilderness

00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:37.990
Earth Engine, expand!
